0.text:
 cattery is a collection of 262 Nix modules for NixOS, nix-darwin, and home-manager. The modules are grouped into rooms: named sets of modules that enable each other with shared defaults. Enable a room to turn on a group of related features, then override the individual modules you want to change. # flake.nix
{
  inputs.cattery-modules.url = "https://flakehub.com/f/nixcafe/cattery-modules/*.tar.gz";

  outputs = { nixpkgs, cattery-modules, ... }: {
    nixosConfigurations.myhost = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      modules = [ cattery-modules.nixosModules.default ];
    };
  };
} # configuration.nix
{ config, ... }: {
  cattery.room.desktop.dev.enable = true;
} cattery.room.desktop.dev enables the desktop chain and a set of developer tools. See Rooms for the full contents of each room.

4.text:
 The flake exports a module set for each platform: # NixOS
imports = [ cattery-modules.nixosModules.default ];

# home-manager
imports = [ cattery-modules.homeModules.default ];

# nix-darwin
imports = [ cattery-modules.darwinModules.default ];

