64.text:
 If you do not want a room, enable modules directly: {
  cattery = {
    desktop.hyprland.enable = true;
    desktop.addons.catppuccin.enable = true;
    services.tailscale.enable = true;
    cli-apps.dev-kit.git.enable = true;
    cli-apps.dev-kit.rust.enable = true;
    cli-apps.shell.fish.enable = true;
    user.name = "alice";
  };
}

65.text:
 Room sub-module enables use lib.mkDefault, so you can turn individual modules off or on: {
  cattery = {
    room.desktop.dev.enable = true;

    # Override room defaults:
    cli-apps.dev-kit.javascript.enable = false; # use bun standalone
    desktop.hyprland.enable = false;
    desktop.niri.enable = true;
  };
}

66.text:
 Several modules read cattery.user for defaults, including git identity, email, GPG, and the login shell: { pkgs, ... }: {
  cattery.user = {
    name = "alice";
    realName = "Alice";
    email = {
      address = "alice@example.com";
      userName = "alice";
    };
    defaultUserShell = pkgs.fish; # also enables the fish module by default
    gpg.signKey = "ABCD1234";
  };
} cattery.user.home, uid, and gid are read-only values taken from the system user.

72.text:
 room.basis plus services.acme. It also exposes qemu-guest.enable and cloud-init.enable. Both are off by default. cattery.room.server-mini.enable = true;
cattery.room.server-mini.qemu-guest.enable = true;
cattery.room.server-mini.cloud-init.enable = true;

73.text:
 room.basis plus room.server-mini. The qemu-guest and cloud-init options are passed through to server-mini. cattery.room.server = {
  enable = true;
  qemu-guest.enable = true;
  cloud-init.enable = true;
};

74.text:
 room.server plus a set of storage and monitoring services. samba, avahi, samba-wsdd, sanoid, syncoid, beszel, nfs, and target are enabled by default. netdata and zfs are available but off by default. zfs requires networking.hostId. cattery.room.server.nas = {
  enable = true;
  zfs.enable = true;
  netdata.enable = false;
};

89.text:
 room.desktop.general plus apps.instant-messengers, apps.jetbrains, apps.code-cursor, cli-apps.database.sqlite, cli-apps.operations.cloud, cli-apps.operations.kubernetes, cli-apps.security.gnupg, and cli-apps.tool.ollama. It also enables cli-apps.video.visual and cli-apps.video.youtube. On Linux it enables apps.thunderbird, apps.science, apps.video, cli-apps.cloudflared, and cli-apps.warp. On Darwin it enables apps.iina and cli-apps.android. The allDevKit option enables cli-apps.dev-kit.cpp, dive, go, java (with Maven and Gradle), javascript, lua, rust, and wasm. cattery.room.desktop.dev = {
  enable = true;
  allDevKit = true;
};

95.text:
 All rooms use lib.mkDefault for sub-module enables, so explicit configuration wins: cattery.room.desktop.dev.enable = true;

cattery.desktop.hyprland.enable = false;
cattery.desktop.niri.enable = true;          # use niri
cattery.apps.jetbrains.enable = false;        # use neovim
cattery.cli-apps.shell.fish.enable = false;
cattery.cli-apps.shell.zsh.enable = true; The login shell modules also read cattery.user.defaultUserShell. Setting that to pkgs.fish, pkgs.zsh, or pkgs.nushell enables the matching module by default.

96.text:
 Rooms can be enabled together. Shared dependencies are enabled once, and each room adds its own modules: cattery = {
  room.desktop.dev.enable = true;
  room.desktop.game.enable = true;
};

101.text:
 Most modules follow this shape: {
  config,
  lib,
  namespace,
  pkgs,
  ...
}:
let
  cfg = config.${namespace}.my-module;
in
{
  options.${namespace}.my-module = {
    enable = lib.mkEnableOption "my module";
    # ... other options
  };

  config = lib.mkIf cfg.enable {
    # ... implementation
  };
}

110.text:
 {
  cattery.secrets.enable = true;
} enable installs the agenix CLI and generates age.secrets from the configured files. cattery.secrets.secretsDir and cattery.secrets.secretsMountPoint are passed to agenix when set.

111.text:
 Most companion modules enable themselves when both the parent service and cattery.secrets are enabled: cattery = {
  secrets.enable = true;

  services.nginx.enable = true;      # encrypted nginx conf.d files
  services.forgejo.enable = true;    # encrypted Forgejo app.ini when useWizard is set
  services.postgresql.enable = true; # encrypted PostgreSQL config when useWizard is set
  services.wg-quick = {
    enable = true;
    configNames = [ "wg0" ];
  };
  services.cloudflared.enable = true; # encrypted tunnel credentials
}; For services with a host configuration file, set useWizard = true on the service to use the encrypted file instead of declarative settings. cattery.nix.secrets is different: it is disabled by default. Set cattery.nix.secrets.enable = true to add the encrypted include to nix.extraOptions.

114.text:
 Generate an age identity if you do not already have one: mkdir -p ~/.config/age
age-keygen -o ~/.config/age/keys.txt If age-keygen is not installed, use nix run nixpkgs#age -- keygen -o ~/.config/age/keys.txt. Add the public key to secrets.nix. The file lists each encrypted file and its recipients: # secrets.nix
{
  "hosts/server/global/nginx.conf.age".publicKeys = [ alice server ];
} Encrypt the file. Run the command from the directory that contains secrets.nix: cd ~/agenix
nix run github:ryantm/agenix -- -e hosts/server/global/nginx.conf.age If you set cattery.secrets.secretsPath = ./secrets, run the same command from that directory. Add the identity to the host. On NixOS, agenix reads the host SSH keys by default. To use the key generated in step 1: {
  age.identityPaths = [ "/home/alice/.config/age/keys.txt" ];
} Enable the service and the secrets module: cattery = {
  secrets.enable = true;
  services.nginx.enable = true;
}; The file is decrypted during activation and linked to its target, for example /etc/nginx/conf.d/nginx.conf.

116.text:
 When cattery.system.impermanence.enable is set on NixOS, the module persists /etc/ssh and sets age.identityPaths to the copies under /persistent/etc/ssh. The host keys used by agenix then survive reboots. Decrypted secrets stay in the agenix runtime directory (normally /run/agenix); the impermanence module does not copy them to the persistent volume. cattery = {
  secrets.enable = true;
  system.impermanence.enable = true;
};
